00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:26,680
Otherwise, we'll never be able
to fall in love,"

241
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:28,933
while others just want to move forward.

242
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,184
- Right.
- They want love.

243
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,352
- They want love.
- Hmm.

244
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:32,728
- There's not much time.
- Exactly.

245
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:34,605
It's a battle between these two sides.

246
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:36,690
- Wow.
- Yeah, that makes a lot of sense.

247
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:08,514
LOVE DINER

248
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:09,682
What are we making?

249
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:11,559
What shall we make?

250
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:13,060
What are we eating?

251
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:21,819
Bo just guesses the amount
of rice he puts in the measuring cup.

252
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:23,946
What's the point of using it?

253
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:26,824
So rice.

254
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:29,034
Right. Carrots and…

255
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:31,287
<i>A car? </i>

256
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:33,372
<i>No way! What?</i>

257
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:35,666
- <i>You've gotta be kidding.</i>
- <i>Our idol!</i>

258
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:39,253
- Right? Yeah, potatoes…
- Yeah.

259
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,255
And these?

260
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:42,715
MR. HENTONA

261
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:44,091
Hey, everybody!

262
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:45,384
My God!

263
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:46,635
- Ma-chan!
- What?

264
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,971
- Mr. Hentona!
- No way!

265
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:50,097
Hentona!

266
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,057
He always comes at the right time.

267
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,267
Hey, guys!

268
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,227
- Oh, the bananas!
- Oh, bananas!

269
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:57,062
I brought bananas. I wanted to see you.

270
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,189
- Give me half.
- Check this.

271
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:00,900
- So good.
- Delicious, right?

272
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:02,985
- The most delicious I've ever had.
- It is.

273
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,946
- Yeah. Uh, wait.
- So good!

274
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,701
I was worried about you guys,
but y'all look like you're good.

275
00:15:10,784 --> 00:15:13,913
- We're doing well.
- Thank you so much, Mr. Hentona.

276
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,623
You look a little down.

277
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:16,874
<i>He noticed right away!</i>

278
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:18,667
- I'll tell you later.
- Oh, okay.

279
00:15:21,211 --> 00:15:23,172
The other day, you were…

280
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:24,924
You were the only one
who didn't look happy.

281
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,717
So I was worried.

282
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,594
I see. Well, thank you.

283
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:32,806
All right.

284
00:15:33,432 --> 00:15:34,433
All right.

285
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,435
It's so beautiful, isn't it?

286
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:37,686
- It is.
- Yeah.

287
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:42,566
So, that day at the banana farm,
you said that

288
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:45,277
- a man who is abusive is no good.
- Uh-huh.

289
00:15:45,361 --> 00:15:47,446
All the men I've dated have been abusive.

290
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:51,158
I was wondering, like,
how do I meet someone who isn't like that?

291
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:52,993
- Hmm.
- I find it so hard.

292
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:55,496
Even though I've, you know,

293
00:15:56,121 --> 00:15:57,748
been alive for 60 years…

294
00:15:57,831 --> 00:15:59,750
- Hmm.
- …I still fail all the time.

295
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:01,919
But, you know, failure is…

296
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:04,630
- Aren't you afraid of failing?
- …Half-- No.

297
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:07,174
- You fail 'cause you take on challenges.
- Hmm.

298
00:16:07,257 --> 00:16:08,133
- Right?
- Hmm.

299
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:10,636
Taking on a challenge
means you're halfway to success.

300
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,846
- It's not a failure.
- Mmm-hmm.

301
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,599
- Understand? Yes.
- It's important to challenge yourself.

302
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:18,352
So, all of the experiences
that you've had with men,

303
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:21,689
all of the men you've met,
all of them have been abusive, right?

304
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:24,274
- These become life experiences for you.
- Hmm.

305
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:26,402
So, eventually, you'll be able to tell,

306
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:29,613
"Oh, this type of guy
is probably abusive."

307
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,198
- Hmm.
- I also want to make sure

308
00:16:31,281 --> 00:16:33,200
- I tell the guys this. You know?
- Yeah.

309
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:36,620
Your looks and appearance
are just given to you by your parents.

310
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:38,163
- Hmm.
- They're from birth.

311
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:41,291
And we should be grateful for that.
You should be grateful to your parents.

312
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:43,377
But we create our inner selves.

313
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:47,506
Hmm. Well, I'm half Japanese,
so I have a mixed background.

314
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:50,718
And I've always been bullied
because of the way I look.

315
00:16:50,801 --> 00:16:52,011
My mom, kind of…

316
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,721
Well, she abandoned me.

317
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:57,558
And my dad, well,
he's always lived overseas, so…

318
00:16:57,641 --> 00:16:59,768
- I've never lived with my parents.
- Mmm.

319
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:01,770
And since I don't have parents around,

320
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,897
it's like I'm searching for love
I don't know.

321
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:05,274
The past is the past.

322
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:07,317
- It's over.
- Hmm.

323
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:09,653
But it also lives on in the future.

324
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:11,488
You've had a hard time, you know?

325
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,656
In other words,

326
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:15,701
the fact that
you didn't receive much love,

327
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:18,245
- that's also an experience.
- Hmm.

328
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:20,539
And when you yourself become a mother,

329
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:21,915
I think you'll be a good mother

330
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:24,168
who can give more love
than your mother did.

331
00:17:24,251 --> 00:17:26,378
- Mmm-hmm.
- You'll give as much as you've suffered.

332
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:29,631
I'm really worried that
since I didn't grow up in a loving home,

333
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,467
it could mean that if I have a kid…

334
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:34,553
if I have a kid,
I won't be able to love them,

335
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:36,430
because I wasn't taught.

336
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,850
- Hmm.
- So, first, you have to love yourself.

337
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:46,273
Like I said,
the fact you were born into this world

338
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:48,275
is already a miracle in itself.

339
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:50,736
And by chance,
you were able to come to Okinawa.

340
00:17:50,819 --> 00:17:53,113
- Yeah.
- This is also like fate.

341
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:55,824
- Hmm.
- All these things, one by one,

342
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:58,243
will make up your life experiences.

343
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,372
It sounds positive
when you put it that way.

344
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:05,667
- Hmm.
- Like, I feel like I can be positive now.

345
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:09,088
- Yeah, you can.
- I used to wonder if my negativity

346
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:12,800
was just caused
by everything from my past.

347
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:15,511
You said you can't change the past,
but you can change the future.

348
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:18,180
- You can change it, you can.
- I'm so glad I got to talk to you.

349
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:19,890
- Thank you, Mr. Hentona.
- Of course.

350
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:23,185
So that's why you should
just go ahead and do…

351
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:25,938
- Yeah. I'll do that.
- …what you want to do.

352
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:28,357
After talking to you, Mr. Hentona,

353
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:32,986
I feel like I'm not really that scared
of failing anymore and stuff like that.

354
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,988
- Hmm.
- I've got a lot more courage.

355
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,323
You'll be fine.

356
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:39,326
- Just remember all your experiences here…
- Hmm.

357
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:40,536
…and feel free to come back.

358
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:41,995
- I understand.
- Anytime.

359
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:44,373
- I'll come back if something bad happens.
- Of course.

360
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:45,624
And I'll say, "Welcome back."

361
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:47,167
Nobody's ever said "welcome back"

362
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:48,544
- to me before.
- Oh, really?

363
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:50,587
It feels like I have a home
for the first time.

364
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:51,964
Come anytime.

365
00:18:52,756 --> 00:18:55,092
You're free to do anything.
You can do anything.

366
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:57,010
- Yeah. Thank you so much.
- Okay?

367
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:59,096
- And if you get really tired…
- Yeah.

368
00:18:59,179 --> 00:19:00,848
- …come back here.
- Okay, got it.

369
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:06,228
<i>I want to choose love.</i>

370
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:08,188
<i>I want to become stronger.</i>

371
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:10,482
<i>I want to tell everybody how I feel.</i>

372
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:13,193
I want to be loved, even if I'm like this.

373
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:17,197
And I came here to find love,
no matter what form it takes.

374
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:20,242
Like, I want to be friends with everybody.

375
00:19:20,325 --> 00:19:22,452
If you take a step, you're halfway there.

376
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:27,040
I want to trust that,
and then it'll help me move in my own way.

377
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,542
'Cause this is who I am.

378
00:19:36,758 --> 00:19:39,386
<i>Four days until the confessions.</i>

379
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:45,017
<i>Today, the weather is good,</i>
<i>so we have prepared a barbecue.</i>

380
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:50,355
<i>At the barbecue,</i>
<i>please deepen your relationships together.</i>

381
00:19:54,484 --> 00:19:55,652
It's chilly.

382
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:10,000
- Let's eat. I'm hungry.
- I have something.

383
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,668
- Can I go first?
- Yeah, sure.

384
00:20:11,752 --> 00:20:13,170
- I'll go first.
- Yes.

385
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:14,296
Let her speak.

386
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,839
I'm sorry about the fact

387
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:19,051
that I couldn't talk properly yesterday
because I was crying.

388
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:23,180
And, like, the things you all said to me,

389
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:27,559
I totally get why you said them,
and, like, I want to try to make a change.

390
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:31,605
I'm going to try, but I'd also
like you all to meet me halfway.

391
00:20:31,688 --> 00:20:33,565
So can you please be friends with me?

392
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:34,816
- Okay!
- All right!

393
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,778
- Of course, we'll meet you halfway.
- I want to say something too.

394
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:41,865
When I went to the guys' room,
I was kind of confrontational.

395
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:45,786
And I wasn't considerate of your feelings
when I talked to you guys.

396
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:48,163
So I'm sorry that I made you feel upset.

397
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:50,457
- It's okay.
- Please be friends with me.

398
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:52,918
- Hey, be friends with us too.
- We'd love to be friends.

399
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:55,045
- We want to be friends.
- Let's do it.

400
00:20:55,128 --> 00:20:56,880
- Let's grill this meat.
- <i>Great.</i>

401
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,465
<i>She's great at apologizing.</i>

402
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,803
Huh?
Does anybody want something to drink or…

403
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:05,430
- Oh, wow, crab!
- Here we go. Boom!

404
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:09,434
It's too peaceful.

405
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:12,020
- It's burning.
- Shit, it's already charred black!

406
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:13,730
- Oh, this is bad.
- What are you doing?

407
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:16,149
- I'm supervising.
- Oh.

408
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:21,029
- <i>They're smiling again.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

409
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:23,907
- Wow, that's amazing!
- Yeah, I know.

410
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:28,161
Hey, the tide is low today.

411
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:30,247
Oh, my God, this might be good.

412
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,040
Let's play catch.

413
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,001
Here I go.

414
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:42,050
Oh, my God, I'm scared.

415
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:46,888
Hey, if…

416
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:49,308
If we don't catch it,
we'll get wet, right?

417
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:50,392
Here I go!

418
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:53,854
Oh, my God.

419
00:21:53,937 --> 00:21:56,106
- <i>Looks fun.</i>
- <i>That's sweet.</i>

420
00:21:57,441 --> 00:22:00,110
You know when we talked
in the living room yesterday?

421
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:01,320
Uh-huh, yeah.

422
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:03,613
It made me realize
something about you, Hikaru.

423
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:04,740
How do I say this?

424
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:07,868
At first, I didn't like
how cautious you were.

425
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:10,954
Like, I was thinking,
"We don't have much time left,

426
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:12,581
you gotta make a decision."

427
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:15,667
But then, Maririn said
she wanted to get to know everyone,

428
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:17,919
so she told them
she was interested in them.

429
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:19,629
When she said that, I was like,

430
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:23,800
"I'd actually hate it if Hikaru tried
to get to know people that way."

431
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:28,847
Like, I'd hate it if you told everyone
you were interested in them,

432
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:30,640
or, like, if you touched them.

433
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:32,976
So now I actually think
it's an amazing thing

434
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:36,396
that you're taking your time
and you're being cautious.

435
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,231
Like, I think that's much better.

436
00:22:38,315 --> 00:22:41,651
- I didn't realize that before, but--
- So you realized that because of Maririn?

437
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:43,070
I did, yeah.

438
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,989
I wrote something.

439
00:22:46,948 --> 00:22:48,367
Hey, where did you…

440
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:49,868
- That letter…
- I brought this from home.

441
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:51,036
The paper's different, right?

442
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:53,246
<i>Yeah, so I brought this paper from home</i>

443
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,665
<i>- to write a letter to someone special.</i>
<i>- You brought it?</i>

444
00:22:57,334 --> 00:22:59,419
Are you laughing?

445
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:00,504
DEAR HIKARU

446
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:01,588
WASSUP?

447
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:02,672
THIS IS MY THIRD LETTER,

448
00:23:02,756 --> 00:23:04,925
BUT I WROTE AGAIN BECAUSE
I WANTED TO TELL YOU HOW I FEEL

449
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,843
Mmm-hmm…

450
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:09,137
What do you mean, "Mm-hmm…"?

451
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,848
Everybody's just using the school's paper.

452
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:15,602
But I wanted to write my letter
to someone special on my own paper.

453
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:18,772
They say that this paper brings happiness.

454
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:22,818
- You don't like it?
- No, it's the best.

455
00:23:22,901 --> 00:23:23,777
- The best?
- Yeah.

456
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:25,362
It's the best.

457
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:27,197
You feel fired up?

458
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:32,744
- Can I give you a kiss?
- You're going too fast!

459
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:36,331
Come on, it's fine.

460
00:23:40,377 --> 00:23:41,878
Are we allowed to smoke here?

461
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,218
Oh, so you can sit here.

462
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:50,011
- You good? You tired?
- Hmm?

463
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,471
- Are you tired?
- Yeah.

464
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:52,681
Hmm, I thought so.

465
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:55,475
- I'm the oldest one here.
- Hmm.

466
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:58,311
I've to look at the bigger picture
and think about more things.

467
00:23:58,395 --> 00:23:59,396
Yeah, I guess so.

468
00:23:59,479 --> 00:24:01,189
I thought,
"Whatever, it's too much trouble."

469
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:02,524
Hmm, I get it.

470
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:06,695
But I'm more mature than you,
so you don't have to be so uptight.

471
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:09,072
I'm probably more mature.

472
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:11,491
- Really? You think that?
- Yeah.

473
00:24:12,659 --> 00:24:13,827
Did you calm down?

474
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:16,496
- Yeah, after I slept.
- Mmm.

475
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:19,791
- Let's switch gears.
- Yeah, okay.

476
00:24:20,709 --> 00:24:22,669
- We don't have much time.
- For real.

477
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:26,089
You see how important sleep is?

478
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,132
That's what it is.

479
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:28,925
- They just gave us a lesson.
- Yeah.

480
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:31,428
