713
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:17,597
- Mmm. Right?
- Yeah.

714
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:20,558
Men can be weak-minded.
Always, like, "What should I do?"

715
00:34:20,641 --> 00:34:22,977
It's amazing how you can get so into it.

716
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:24,771
Well, I've made up my mind.

717
00:34:26,105 --> 00:34:27,607
Women are more manly than men.

718
00:34:27,690 --> 00:34:30,026
I've always thought that.

719
00:34:30,693 --> 00:34:33,029
This is definitely
a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

720
00:34:33,112 --> 00:34:35,948
- Yeah.
- So we should throw ourselves into it.

721
00:34:38,326 --> 00:34:42,371
Like, I thought Ruru was nice,
but I only know her through other people.

722
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:44,248
Yeah, I don't know
what kind of person she is.

723
00:34:44,332 --> 00:34:45,333
- Hmm.
- So…

724
00:34:46,167 --> 00:34:49,545
So I thought it was important to just
let go of it all and try talking to her.

725
00:34:49,629 --> 00:34:51,380
Hmm. You're right.

726
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:54,717
Will you put in the effort?

727
00:34:56,844 --> 00:34:58,054
Yeah, I think I can.

728
00:35:00,389 --> 00:35:03,226
This was an important first step.
Like, for me.

729
00:35:03,309 --> 00:35:05,478
- Hmm.
- I mean, this type of conversation.

730
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:07,271
- Yeah, that's right.
- Yeah.

731
00:35:08,356 --> 00:35:10,566
- You took a step forward.
- Yeah.

732
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:12,151
- Thank you.
- Hmm.

733
00:35:13,986 --> 00:35:17,073
<i>I thought</i>
<i>I wanted to talk to Ruru. You know?</i>

734
00:35:17,657 --> 00:35:21,035
You don't get many opportunities
to be on a show like <i>Badly In Love.</i>

735
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:22,954
And meeting someone from Tokyo,

736
00:35:23,037 --> 00:35:25,581
whose base of operations
is so close to mine,

737
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:27,750
it's also kind of like fate, no?

738
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:30,378
<i>I really like Ruru's smile.</i>

739
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:32,839
<i>My favorite thing to do</i>
<i>is watch her from behind</i>

740
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:36,259
<i>while she's laughing</i>
<i>and watching TV or something.</i>

741
00:35:36,342 --> 00:35:40,221
<i>And the reason I do that is because</i>
<i>I like girls who laugh out loud.</i>

742
00:35:40,304 --> 00:35:43,766
I really want to honor
this kind of fate and destiny,

743
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:47,228
and I want to tell her
that I want to believe in it.

744
00:35:47,311 --> 00:35:48,312
It's a kind of…

745
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:51,858
It's not persuasion,
but it's a kind of pick-up line.

746
00:35:52,775 --> 00:35:56,154
I'll use that kind of thing
to gradually make it more realistic.

747
00:35:57,113 --> 00:35:59,907
If I have more opportunities with her,
I'll succeed.

748
00:36:07,623 --> 00:36:09,250
- Ruru, let's talk.
- Sure.

749
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:13,713
- We talked a little bit in the sauna.
- Mmm.

750
00:36:13,796 --> 00:36:15,756
I think we've had
the most opportunities to talk.

751
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:16,924
- Mmm.
- Right.

752
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,801
That's why, like, after all of that,

753
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:21,012
the fact that
you're set on Leo is kind of…

754
00:36:22,930 --> 00:36:26,726
I mean, it's not like I'm angry about it,
but I do feel kind of lonely.

755
00:36:26,809 --> 00:36:28,811
- Mmm.
- Yeah. Like, "What?"

756
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:31,772
Well, I try to be realistic, you know?

757
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:34,025
- Hmm.
- I think really deeply about things.

758
00:36:34,650 --> 00:36:36,903
He's in Kyoto, and I'm in Tokyo.

759
00:36:36,986 --> 00:36:40,406
I'm not made for long-distance.
Personally.

760
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:44,410
Not being able to see each other
when you want to, it's like…

761
00:36:44,493 --> 00:36:46,162
Right. Yeah, I really think that.

762
00:36:46,245 --> 00:36:48,873
But I think it's impossible for me
to be with anyone else.

763
00:36:48,956 --> 00:36:51,375
- Mmm.
- I want to have a realistic relationship.

764
00:36:51,459 --> 00:36:53,961
I want to have a proper relationship
when I leave here.

765
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,672
- We're the only ones in Tokyo, aren't we?
- Yeah, that's right.

766
00:36:57,173 --> 00:37:00,009
That's something I think about,
and it's a huge thing for me.

767
00:37:00,092 --> 00:37:02,595
I have the money
to take the bullet train anytime.

768
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:05,765
So I could go see him,
but I have limited time.

769
00:37:05,848 --> 00:37:08,893
And I have work, too.
So when I think about that reality…

770
00:37:09,477 --> 00:37:12,897
I start thinking, "That's not gonna work,"
and I start to doubt.

771
00:37:13,731 --> 00:37:16,067
So I'm the only one.

772
00:37:16,150 --> 00:37:19,153
That's true.
Well, distance-wise, that's true.

773
00:37:20,196 --> 00:37:23,199
Before I came here,
as long as I could move my thumbs,

774
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:25,826
I would tell girls how I felt with a text.

775
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:28,746
I'd tell them half-heartedly,
and they'd kind of accept it,

776
00:37:28,829 --> 00:37:30,873
and I had a lot
of half-hearted relationships.

777
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:34,418
But being here,
I have to look them in the eye, you know?

778
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:37,255
I have to look them in the eye
and tell them how I feel,

779
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:39,548
and I have to keep telling them
how I feel.

780
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:43,261
Otherwise, if I do things half-heartedly,
it's not that I think I'd lose,

781
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:46,055
but I don't think
that they'd accept my feelings.

782
00:37:46,639 --> 00:37:47,890
So I think I've changed.

783
00:37:48,683 --> 00:37:50,184
<i>I look them in the eye now.</i>

784
00:37:50,726 --> 00:37:53,562
<i>And I tell them</i>
<i>how I feel with my actual words.</i>

785
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:58,401
I believe that doing things that way
is very important and also very powerful.

786
00:38:00,695 --> 00:38:03,114
So I thought I'd talk to you.

787
00:38:03,197 --> 00:38:05,950
I don't know about your past,
so I wanted to ask you about that.

788
00:38:06,033 --> 00:38:08,119
My past isn't anything special,
to be honest.

789
00:38:08,202 --> 00:38:11,414
I got arrested at the end
of my first year of junior high.

790
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:12,498
For what?

791
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:15,584
- 'Cause I got into a fight.
- Okay. Mmm.

792
00:38:15,668 --> 00:38:16,919
They assessed me.

793
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:19,922
And the first time, I just got sent back.

794
00:38:21,090 --> 00:38:22,216
I came back.

795
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:26,470
Then, about a year later,
I got arrested again.

796
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:28,764
- For fighting? Uh-huh.
- Yeah.

797
00:38:28,848 --> 00:38:31,475
And then, I went
to the juvenile training center.

798
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:33,978
I came back at the end of the third year,

799
00:38:34,061 --> 00:38:36,063
three months
before graduating junior high.

800
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:38,524
Then six months later,
I was back at the center.

801
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,609
Hey, you know,

802
00:38:40,693 --> 00:38:43,487
I've actually been violent
in the past as well.

803
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:44,405
Yeah?

804
00:38:44,488 --> 00:38:46,907
I got into fist fights
with my ex and stuff.

805
00:38:47,408 --> 00:38:51,579
Did you ever regret it afterwards?
Like, after you were ever violent?

806
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:56,167
I did regret it.
Or I don't know if it was regret.

807
00:38:56,250 --> 00:38:58,377
- More like a reflection?
- But I did reflect on it.

808
00:38:58,919 --> 00:39:00,087
I mean, it's like…

809
00:39:01,213 --> 00:39:03,549
You gotta think
about the future a little more.

810
00:39:03,632 --> 00:39:06,385
When you start dating people
at this age, you know?

811
00:39:06,469 --> 00:39:09,055
Yeah, you don't wanna be with someone
who's gonna get arrested.

812
00:39:09,138 --> 00:39:10,848
Yeah, for real.

813
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:12,641
Yeah, that's exactly it.

814
00:39:12,725 --> 00:39:13,976
If they go to prison,

815
00:39:14,852 --> 00:39:18,105
you can't, like, just ask them
what they're thinking whenever you want.

816
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:20,524
- And you can't see them when you want.
- Yeah.

817
00:39:20,608 --> 00:39:23,402
You also feel bad
for making the other person wait.

818
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:25,196
But that bit was my fault, so…

819
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:27,490
Everyone who gets arrested says that.

820
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:29,075
"Everyone who gets arrested says that."

821
00:39:29,158 --> 00:39:31,494
- As if it's something really common.
- It is a common thing.

822
00:39:32,078 --> 00:39:34,580
So, if the two of us were to start dating,

823
00:39:34,663 --> 00:39:37,541
I would want you to know
that you can't do those things

824
00:39:37,625 --> 00:39:39,001
because I'm here.

825
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:41,128
For sure. I don't want to get arrested.

826
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:44,507
Not that I want to do anything bad.

827
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:47,343
But also, you have to accept
the bad parts too.

828
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:53,391
- That's how I think a relationship works.
- I get it. To what extent? Okay.

829
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:56,394
It's easy to notice the bad parts
more than the good parts.

830
00:39:56,477 --> 00:39:58,396
- That's true.
- Which means that you fight more often.

831
00:39:58,479 --> 00:40:00,398
When you're dating, that's how it is.

832
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:04,777
So then you just have to think about
how you can change that.

833
00:40:04,860 --> 00:40:06,445
<i>They understand each other.</i>

834
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:08,697
I want to cherish the person
closest to me.

835
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:11,617
- <i>Bo never talks this much.</i>
- <i>You're right, he doesn't.</i>

836
00:40:13,661 --> 00:40:16,997
It's all about compassion.
I want someone who's really deep.

837
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:19,125
Well, I'm deep.

838
00:40:19,208 --> 00:40:20,793
Really?

839
00:40:20,876 --> 00:40:22,753
- You said you're deep.
- I'm deep.

840
00:40:22,837 --> 00:40:24,463
- <i>Nice.</i>
- <i>Good.</i>

841
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:25,840
Hmm.

842
00:40:25,923 --> 00:40:30,928
In my past relationships,
I always wanted someone I could rely on.

843
00:40:31,011 --> 00:40:33,973
Someone who understood me
and accepted every part of me.

844
00:40:35,182 --> 00:40:39,395
That's what I thought when I was dating.
But it was a total failure.

845
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:41,939
Because they always ended up lying to me.

846
00:40:42,022 --> 00:40:44,733
They'd say that
they hadn't done anything illegal.

847
00:40:45,651 --> 00:40:47,445
I'd ask them to swear to me.

848
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:51,449
They'd swear to me,
but then they'd end up in prison.

849
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:55,453
They'd tell me
that they'd already divorced their wife.

850
00:40:55,536 --> 00:40:57,329
But then I'd find out they hadn't.

851
00:40:58,038 --> 00:41:01,500
I think that through this experience
we've had in here,

852
00:41:02,501 --> 00:41:06,172
Bo's apologized honestly and sincerely,
and I see that.

853
00:41:08,883 --> 00:41:10,259
I don't think that he lied.

854
00:41:11,302 --> 00:41:14,263
If he's lied, then I won't be able
to trust anyone again.

855
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:15,848
Well, I think that every time.

856
00:41:15,931 --> 00:41:19,268
That's how much I truly believe
that Bo wouldn't lie.

857
00:41:19,351 --> 00:41:20,519
I don't think he would.

858
00:41:20,603 --> 00:41:22,813
I think he's the one I trust the most
out of the guys.

859
00:41:22,897 --> 00:41:26,400
'Cause, you know,
he also shows you his bad side first.

860
00:41:27,610 --> 00:41:29,403
That's why I think he wouldn't lie.

861
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:31,572
If I had to choose,

862
00:41:33,115 --> 00:41:34,116
it would be Bo.

863
00:41:35,326 --> 00:41:36,327
<i>That's great.</i>

864
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:38,996
<i>It seems like</i>
<i>her feelings are already set.</i>

865
00:41:56,972 --> 00:41:58,307
<i>A bento box.</i>

866
00:42:02,102 --> 00:42:03,979
- What's up?
- Oh, you're late.

867
00:42:04,063 --> 00:42:05,439
Oh, what is it?

868
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:07,358
- Well, I wanted to talk.
- Okay.

869
00:42:12,488 --> 00:42:13,614
- So, what--
- I made you a bento.

870
00:42:13,697 --> 00:42:15,449
- No way! Seriously?
- Yeah.

871
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:17,743
- No way!
- <i>They're so cute.</i>

872
00:42:17,826 --> 00:42:19,912
I've never made a bento box
for a guy before.

873
00:42:19,995 --> 00:42:22,039
That's crazy. It's hot! Thank you.

874
00:42:22,122 --> 00:42:24,166
- <i>How nice.</i>
- Can I eat this?

875
00:42:24,250 --> 00:42:26,669
- Yeah. Have you eaten?
- No, not yet.

876
00:42:26,752 --> 00:42:28,170
Thanks for the food.

877
00:42:29,463 --> 00:42:30,923
<i>They look really good together.</i>

878
00:42:31,006 --> 00:42:32,258
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- <i>Simply put.</i>

879
00:42:32,341 --> 00:42:33,342
Mmm.

880
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:35,553
- It's delicious!
- Is it good?

881
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:37,096
- It's delicious!
- Glad to hear that.

882
00:42:37,179 --> 00:42:38,556
It's really good.

883
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:41,225
I didn't even taste it.
I didn't have time.

884
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:43,727
Yeah, it's so good. Like, so, so good.

885
00:42:43,811 --> 00:42:45,479
- So you've never done this before?
- Never.

886
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:47,565
- It's your first time? Very first time?
- It is. Uh-huh.

887
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:50,192
This is actually so great. Oh, my God!

888
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:52,403
- Ma-kun is so cute, isn't he?
- Right?

889
00:42:52,486 --> 00:42:54,196
- It's unexpected.
- Yeah.

890
00:42:54,780 --> 00:42:58,909
I mean, I've made bento boxes before,
but I just ate them all myself.

891
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:02,121
- Mmm.
- I've never made one for someone else.

892
00:43:02,204 --> 00:43:05,749
Mmm. Yeah, it's delicious.
Really, really good.

893
00:43:05,833 --> 00:43:07,585
It's so warm.

894
00:43:07,668 --> 00:43:09,086
Seriously.

895
00:43:09,169 --> 00:43:11,297
- Thank you. It was so delicious.
- Of course.

896
00:43:12,089 --> 00:43:14,008
Well, I know I've said this before,

897
00:43:14,091 --> 00:43:18,512
but regardless of whether or not
we continue after this experience here,

898
00:43:18,596 --> 00:43:22,099
if we can't continue this relationship,
I don't want to be in a relationship.

899
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:24,602
I don't want it if it's not real.

900
00:43:26,353 --> 00:43:28,063
- Hmm, I understand.
- Hmm.

901
00:43:29,189 --> 00:43:30,190
Is that okay?

902
00:43:31,108 --> 00:43:32,109
It sure is.

903
00:43:38,157 --> 00:43:39,825
What?

904
00:43:39,908 --> 00:43:42,453
- But it was so out of the blue!
- So casual.

905
00:43:42,536 --> 00:43:44,913
Sneaking a nice little daytime kiss.

906
00:43:45,539 --> 00:43:48,500
- But then again, Mr. Ichiro says…
- Oh, I get it now!

907
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:51,337
So it means that her judgment
wouldn't have been affected.

908
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:52,421
Exactly.

909
00:43:52,504 --> 00:43:55,966
I'm embarrassed!

910
00:43:56,050 --> 00:43:57,760
I feel so embarrassed!

911
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:00,679
Oh, that was a delicious bento.

912
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:03,724
BRING ON LIFE

913
00:44:03,807 --> 00:44:06,018
- Sensei, go ahead.
- Go on, Sensei.

914
00:44:06,101 --> 00:44:09,647
Okay, everyone, please put your right
and left hands together like so.

915
00:44:10,689 --> 00:44:12,149
Wassapetit.

916
00:44:12,232 --> 00:44:14,818
- Wassapetit!
- That's a new one.

917
00:44:15,402 --> 00:44:16,612
Is the ajillo good?

918
00:44:16,695 --> 00:44:17,655
- Yeah.
- It's okay now?

919
00:44:17,738 --> 00:44:18,739
- Yeah.
- I'm glad.

920
00:44:18,822 --> 00:44:21,617
- You couldn't eat it before, could you?
- Why not? Is it the taste?

921
00:44:21,700 --> 00:44:24,286
- This is the only thing I don't like.
- Wait, what?

922
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:27,247
- I actually hate carrots.
- I don't like yuzu.

923
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:29,541
I mean, I can eat it, but I don't.

924
00:44:31,043 --> 00:44:32,795
It's time for the evening sauna session.

925
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:35,839
<i>We have prepared for you…</i>

926
00:44:35,923 --> 00:44:39,718
<i>…a two-day and one-night date</i>
<i>that starts tomorrow.</i>

927
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:41,929
Yes, please!

928
00:44:42,012 --> 00:44:43,430
It's a sleepover.

929
00:44:43,514 --> 00:44:44,556
Have we done that before?

930
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:46,183
- No.
- We haven't, have we?

931
00:44:46,266 --> 00:44:49,311
<i>The men will have a serious showdown.</i>

932
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:50,979
<i>The winner will then choose</i>

933
00:44:51,063 --> 00:44:53,565
<i>- the woman he's interested in.</i>
- What do they mean?

934
00:44:55,859 --> 00:45:00,322
<i>The game we will play</i>
<i>will be a real test of guts for the men.</i>

935
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:04,034
<i>Sounds like this test</i>
<i>needs to be won by a real man.</i>

936
00:45:04,118 --> 00:45:05,953
So is this showdown thing tomorrow?

937
00:45:06,036 --> 00:45:07,538
- Yeah.
- They'll tell us more then.

938
00:45:11,041 --> 00:45:12,167
I'm sure I'll win.

939
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:16,130
Piece of cake.
I don't know what it is, but still.

940
00:45:16,213 --> 00:45:17,423
I'm gonna win.

941
00:45:18,132 --> 00:45:19,758
When we had our talk,

942
00:45:19,842 --> 00:45:23,887
Ruru said that if there was a date,
she'd like to go with me.

943
00:45:24,638 --> 00:45:26,306
So I'm going with Ruru.

944
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:30,018
I think tomorrow is gonna be a big event
that will change everything.

945
00:45:30,102 --> 00:45:32,646
If I win tomorrow, I'm choosing Ruru.

946
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:34,106
And I'm going for the win.

947
00:45:34,857 --> 00:45:38,026
Hikaru.
I said that if I win, I'd take her.

948
00:45:38,527 --> 00:45:40,946
I really want to get a kiss. Yeah.

949
00:45:41,029 --> 00:45:43,282
Well, I'm gonna win.

950
00:45:44,575 --> 00:45:47,953
And the person I want to go
on the overnight date with is Hikaru.

951
00:45:48,036 --> 00:45:49,413
I'll do what I have to do.

952
00:45:49,913 --> 00:45:51,290
But it's down to Asuka.

953
00:45:52,708 --> 00:45:54,293
- A sleepover.
- What was that?

954
00:45:54,376 --> 00:45:56,587
- This is huge. Going to be fun.
- Two days and one night means…

955
00:45:56,670 --> 00:45:58,213
Tomorrow night is the night they mean.

956
00:45:58,297 --> 00:45:59,298
Oh, yeah?

957
00:46:00,299 --> 00:46:01,300
Excuse me.

958
00:46:02,468 --> 00:46:05,012
- <i>Huh?</i>
- <i>Wait, what? "Excuse me"?</i>

959
00:46:05,095 --> 00:46:07,264
Listen up, please,
I have something to tell you.

960
00:46:07,765 --> 00:46:09,475
- Whose voice is that?
- That voice!

961
00:46:09,558 --> 00:46:11,059
- Sensei? Right?
- Yes. It's him.

962
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:12,352
- It's been a while.
- Huh?

963
00:46:13,645 --> 00:46:15,564
Huh? What's happening?

964
00:46:17,649 --> 00:46:20,319
A school rule has been broken.

965
00:46:20,402 --> 00:46:21,945
My heart is pounding.

966
00:46:22,571 --> 00:46:26,950
I need to talk with all of you
about this rule violation.

967
00:46:28,410 --> 00:46:30,120
<i>Huh? I don't get it.</i>

968
00:46:39,963 --> 00:46:40,964
What?!

969
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:43,175
What is this?

970
00:46:43,258 --> 00:46:45,385
- I'm so sorry, guys.
- There's more?

971
00:46:46,136 --> 00:46:48,430
- That's enough!
- Yes.

972
00:46:48,514 --> 00:46:50,599
Can I be honest with you? I'm tired.

973
00:46:50,682 --> 00:46:52,768
For real.

974
00:46:52,851 --> 00:46:54,102
Huh?

975
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:56,647
- Sorry.
- That was really scary.

976
00:46:56,730 --> 00:46:58,649
- It was, right?
- I was like, "Who is that?"

977
00:46:58,732 --> 00:46:59,942
So, in Season 1…

978
00:47:00,025 --> 00:47:01,276
- Right!
- The person who came then?

979
00:47:01,360 --> 00:47:02,945
- The one called Yanboh…
- Yeah.

980
00:47:03,028 --> 00:47:05,113
- …was actually Director Kimura.
- I see.

981
00:47:05,197 --> 00:47:07,741
We really didn't think he would have
to make an appearance this time.

982
00:47:07,825 --> 00:47:08,784
I thought so too.

983
00:47:08,867 --> 00:47:11,453
But then, with only three
or four days left…

984
00:47:11,537 --> 00:47:12,663
I see, Mr. Kimura…

985
00:47:12,746 --> 00:47:15,082
We're the ones who are tired here.

986
00:47:15,165 --> 00:47:17,209
- Mr. Kimura must be the most tired.
- The whole staff.

987
00:47:17,292 --> 00:47:18,585
Yeah, but he's the most tired.
